## 7. File Organization & Imports

### 7.1 Directory Ownership

| Directory | Purpose |
|-----------|---------|
| `src/core/` | Stateless business logic (no IO dependencies) |
| `src/mcp-server/handlers/` | MCP tool handlers (thin wrappers) |
| `src/mcp-server/` | Server entrypoint, tool registration, role filtering |
| `src/db/` | Database schema, migrations, queries (Drizzle ORM) |
| `src/schemas/` | Shared Zod validation schemas |
| `extension/src/` | VS Code extension code (commands, views, webviews) |
| `test/{smoke,unit,integration}/` | Tiered test directories (see §6.1) |
| `extension/test/{smoke,unit,integration}/` | Extension tiered tests |
| `testing/` | Legacy integration tests |
| `templates/` | Handlebars templates (`.hbs`) |

### 7.2 Import Order

Organize imports in this order, separated by blank lines:

1. Node.js built-in modules (`node:fs`, `node:path`)
2. External packages (`zod`, `drizzle-orm`, `@modelcontextprotocol/sdk`)
3. Internal absolute imports (`../schemas/config.js`)
4. Internal relative imports (`./errors.js`)

### 7.3 Configuration & Data Files

- **Config/data**: YAML with Zod schema validation (`readYaml(path, Schema)`).
- **Templates**: Handlebars (`.hbs`) in `.orchestra/common/templates/` or `templates/`.
- **Output formats**: Both YAML and Markdown supported via `TemplateFormat`.

